% ---- specification table ----
54 384 545 (SPECIFICATIONS) sechead
/rowY 540 def
(Base model) { (Karpathy's llama2.c stories260K \(trained on TinyStories\), fine-tuned by us on 8,757 printer stories written by Xing4.0-29B-A4B \(Apache-2.0\)) fseg } spec
(Parameters) { (260,032) fseg } spec
(Architecture) { (Llama-2 decoder: 5 layers, dim 64, 8 query heads / 4 KV heads, head size 8, SwiGLU FFN \(hidden 172\), RoPE, RMSNorm) fseg } spec
(Vocabulary) { (512-token SentencePiece) fseg } spec
(Quantization) { (int8 weights, one scale per row; activations in PostScript reals; embedding shared with the output head) fseg } spec
(Context window) { (8.5 \201 11 in. \(512 tokens\)) fseg } spec
(KV cache) { (Persistent, archival, recyclable) fseg } spec
(Job size) { (595 KB, one file:) fseg 8 fC (toner1.ps) fseg 8.2 fH fjoin (. Weights, vocabulary, a forward pass of about 100 lines and its own page layout) fseg } spec
(Speed, measured) { (About 80 tok/s in Ghostscript 10.07 on an Apple-silicon Mac, using 3.3 to 7.5 MB of PostScript VM) fseg } spec
(Speed, printer) { (0.92 tok/s, measured on an HP Color LaserJet Pro MFP M281fdw: 200 tokens in 3:37 by the printer's own clock) fseg } spec
(Time to first token) { (1.7 s on the HP, read back over the network) fseg } spec
(Accelerator) { (The office's hottest inference chip \(fuser, typically about 200 \200C\)) fseg } spec
(Host compute) { (0 FLOPs. The host only sends bytes:) fseg fnl 8 fC (nc <printer-ip> 9100 < toner1.ps) fseg } spec
(Output modality) { (Native toner) fseg } spec
(Open weights) { (Literally. Hex appendix available; OCR to load) fseg } spec
(Pricing) { (Inference cost includes toner) fseg } spec

